; The host CLI. Outside the production closure by construction: it is an
; executable, so nothing can depend on it, and tools/asm-check-purity.sh
; classifies tool/ as a non-production tree. This is where argument parsing and
; file I/O are allowed to live; §9's rule is that none of it leaks back into a
; library.

(executable
 (name asm)
 (modes exe)
 (libraries foundation image target_intf driver fmt))
